"<p>You can claim tax relief from HMRC on professional fees and subscriptions on its approved list, such as the GMC, BMA and Royal College. Tick the ones you pay and Anaesthetic Ally works out the total and the relief, and keeps it up to date as your grade changes.</p><div class=\"expmount\"></div><h4>What you can and can't claim</h4><ul><li>You can claim for the current year and backdate claims for the previous 4 tax years.</li><li>Claim through your HMRC personal tax account; your tax code then goes up so you pay less tax each month.</li><li>Royal College exam fees, including resits, are allowable if you're on a training programme leading to a CCT in that specialty (BMA guidance). Travel and overnight costs for the exam may be too. Revision courses that aren't a contractual requirement are not.</li><li>You can't claim for anything your employer reimburses. In England, resident doctors' Royal College exam fees (first 2 attempts) are reimbursed from April 2026, and College subscriptions are expected to be from April 2027.</li></ul><p class=\"note\">HMRC decides each claim; check the BMA guidance on <a href=\"https://www.bma.org.uk/pay-and-contracts/tax/tax-claim/claiming-for-professional-expenses\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">claiming for professional expenses</a>.</p><p>Sources: <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/tax-relief-for-employees/professional-fees-and-subscriptions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GOV.UK: professional fees and subscriptions</a> · <a href=\"https://www.gmc-uk.org/registration-and-licensing/managing-your-registration/fees-and-funding/fees-for-doctors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GMC fees</a> · <a href=\"https://www.bma.org.uk/join-us/subscription-costs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BMA subscription costs</a> · <a href=\"https://rcoa.ac.uk/examinations/reviews-reports/cost-training\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">RCoA cost of training</a></p>"
